ctedA0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SignedInteger","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SZ"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The length of the edge at a position."}]}],"name":"weight"}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tour, the edges it duplicates (each once per extra copy) and its weight; nil"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when there is none."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each vertex with more edges in than out sends the difference, at each edge’s weight per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy, to the vertices with more out than in: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the network simplex) on the graph, every edge’s capacity the total imbalance. An edge’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flow is the number of times it is duplicated. The walk is Hierholzer’s on the out-rows,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each vertex’s out-edges in position order followed by their copies in position order, from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the first vertex with an edge. Self-loops are walked once and never duplicated. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called once per edge, in position order, before any work.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No weight is negative, and every weight fits in "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the total imbalance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times the sum of the weights fits in "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the flow’s cost bound); the tour’s weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fits in "},{"code":"W","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The network simplex on n vertices and m edges, plus O(n + m + the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"duplicates) for the walk.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest closed walk along every edge at least once, in its direction (the directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Chinese postman problem), by minimum-cost flow (Edmonds and Johnson 1973), or nil when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph has no edge or the vertices with edges are not strongly connected. Isolated vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are ignored."}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"chinesePostmanTour","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","pr